      "abstract": "Between 1910 und 1915 the Hungarian philosopher B\u00e9la Zalai (1882-1915) developed his \u201ccomparative metaphysics of systems\u201d, which had a significant influence on both the young Georg Luk\u00e1cs and also on Karl Mannheim. Through an analysis of Zalai\u2019s approach to metaphysics, we show how he served to mediate between the realist Austrian philosophy of Meinong and of the early Husserl on the one side, and the German (idealistic, Kantian) philosophy then dominant in Hungary.",
